{
    "background_story": "Callan was a fearless warrior from the ancient land of Thrace. Born into a tribe of skilled horsemen and fierce fighters, he was trained from a young age in the art of combat. Callan's bravery and strength in battle earned him a reputation among his people, and he quickly rose through the ranks to become a respected leader. He fought alongside his comrades against the invading armies of Rome, using his knowledge of the rugged Thracian terrain to outmaneuver their foes. Despite being vastly outnumbered, Callan's cunning and valor inspired his troops to fight on, and they achieved several key victories against the Roman legions. His name became synonymous with Thracian courage, and his legacy lived on as a hero of his people.",
